INT. CRUISE SHIP ENGINE ROOM - NIGHT

A cathedral of pipes and gauges. Diesel hammer, steam hiss. Walkways of grated steel overhang a pit where a titanic crankshaft thunders. Heat shimmers the air. Red emergency light.

ROMAN (40s, chief engineer, greasy coverall, wrench in his belt) stands at a panel. BRONWEN (30s, security officer, stiff collar, radio at her hip) paces the catwalk. CAPTAIN MBEKI (50s, white uniform, polished buttons) leans on the rail, hat low. KESTREL (30s, stowaway, hood up, a black duffel bag) crouches by a bulkhead hatch.

ROMAN
Nobody's supposed to be down here.

BRONWEN
That's what I told her.

KESTREL
I told you. I'm lost.

CAPTAIN MBEKI
You are not lost.

The radio at Bronwen's hip crackles.

HARBOR (V.O.)
Ship's engine room, this is Harbor Control. Do you copy?

BRONWEN
(into radio)
Harbor, we copy. Standby.

HARBOR (V.O.)
Be advised, authorities are boarding at dawn.

Mbeki straightens. Kestrel's hand tightens on the duffel. Roman looks from one to the other.

CAPTAIN MBEKI
Who requested the boarding?

HARBOR (V.O.)
Negative. Orders from the flag state.

Kestrel bolts for the ladder. Bronwen vaults the rail and tackles her. They crash on the grating. The duffel bursts open and a stack of sealed documents slides across the floor. Roman scoops up a page and reads the header. Mbeki draws a revolver.

CAPTAIN MBEKI (CONT'D)
Nobody move.

Everyone freezes. Only the engine moves.
